 "description": "\"What's the effect of [variant]\" / \"predict consequences of [genomic change]\" / \"VEP for [chrom:pos]\" \u2014 Variant Effect Predictor for a specified region + allele. Returns consequences (missense, synonymous, splice, etc.), affected genes, transcript impacts, SIFT/PolyPhen predictions. Use for variant interpretation in clinical or research genomics. THE REGION IS REQUIRED \u2014 there is no default. A GRCh37/hg19 position is also a valid GRCh38 position, so an unstated build cannot be detected, only guessed wrong, and a wrong guess returns confident annotations for a DIFFERENT gene rather than an error.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "examples": [
   {
    "allele": "C",
    "assembly": "GRCh38",
    "region": "9:22125504-22125504:1",
    "species": "human"
   },
   {
    "allele": "A",
    "assembly": "GRCh37",
    "region": "1:11856378-11856378:1",
    "species": "human"
   }
  ],
  "properties": {
   "allele": {
    "description": "e.g. \"C\"",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "assembly": {
    "description": "REQUIRED. The genome build your region is in: \"GRCh38\" (= hg38) or \"GRCh37\" (= hg19). There is no default on purpose \u2014 a genomic position is valid in BOTH builds, so an unstated build cannot be detected, only guessed wrong, and a wrong guess returns confident consequence calls for a different gene instead of an error.",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "region": {
    "description": "e.g. \"9:22125504-22125504:1\" \u2014 in the build named by assembly.",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "species": {
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "species",
   "region",
   "allele",
   "assembly"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
